(Individualized, risk-stratified screening intervals for diabetic retinopathy: design and) Tj
T*
(rationale of a large-scale population equivalence trial) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Rationale: Annual screening for diabetic retinopathy imposes substantial resource burden,) Tj
T*
(yet individualized risk assessment might optimize screening intervals while maintaining) Tj
T*
(safety. This equivalence trial evaluates a risk-stratified, variable-interval screening) Tj
T*
(approach versus standard annual screening. Methods: We will enroll 4500+ individuals with) Tj
T*
(diabetes aged 12+ years from an established population-based screening program.) Tj
T*
(Participants will be randomized 1:1 to receive either individualized screening intervals) Tj
T*
(\(6, 12, or 24 months based on baseline and dynamic risk factors\) determined by a validated) Tj
T*
(risk prediction algorithm, or annual screening \(control\). Screening intervals will be) Tj
T*
(adjusted at each visit based on updated risk calculations incorporating demographic,) Tj
T*
(clinical, and prior screening data. Primary outcome is first-visit attendance \(safety) Tj
T*
(measure\). Secondary outcomes include detection rates of sight-threatening retinopathy,) Tj
T*
(quality of life measures, and program costs. The study will employ a two-year minimum) Tj
T*
(follow-up with observer masking of allocation. The equivalence margin for attendance is) Tj
T*
(pre-specified.) Tj
